# F3-REVIEW — DO-NOT-ADVANCE
Specified pytest: 122 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1.26 s). Synthetic reproductions R1–R13 below were executed separately from pytest.
Read-only review on model-v2-explore; only this report written. All findings remain unfixed by task scope; no jobs, sealed data, or outcome files accessed.
- HIGH R1 evaluation_core.py:272: `_as_table` trusts publicly constructible/mutable `ObservationTable`; absent negative evidence still yields AUPRC/AUROC=1, FDR=0, accuracy=1. Revalidate public inputs and make validated rows immutable.
- HIGH R2 evaluation_core.py:750: zero or NaN minimum negatives permits AUPRC/accuracy/FDR with zero negatives. Validate policy counts as finite positive integers and require both classes regardless of configured minimum.
- HIGH R3 evaluation_core.py:235: Holgersen S4 is accepted by default; `responder-only`/`absence from responder list` evade exact-string blacklists and yield AUROC=1. Register known responder-only sources and canonicalize/validate evidence categories.
- HIGH R4 evaluation_core.py:743: ten renamed copies of one positive/negative observation count as ten units per class although `effective_clusters` finds one cluster. Count independent components for metric/PU minima and detect duplicate assay records.
- HIGH R5 evaluation_core.py:529: rows sharing `independent_unit_id` straddle train/test and outer-test/inner folds when other axes differ. Include independent-unit identity in every split's grouping and leakage checks.
- HIGH R6 evaluation_core.py:586: purging sequence bridge B of A~B~C before inner reclustering separates A/C; inner train/test then share the original transitive cluster. Preserve globally established group identities through nesting.
- HIGH R7 evaluation_core.py:435: MOE and 2'-MOE become different groups and straddle train/test. Canonicalize chemistry families using an explicit alias vocabulary; reject ambiguous families.
- HIGH R8 evaluation_core.py:1184: a plan built before sequence/window metadata changes is accepted with identical observation IDs; verification checks stale stored groups. Bind plans to config/data fingerprints and recompute groups before fitting.
- HIGH R9 evaluation_core.py:1181: feature matrices require no provenance and `source_paths=()` permits fitting without feature-source checks. Require validated source manifests covering every feature input before invoking fit_predict.
- MED R10 evaluation_core.py:111: double URL encoding, fullwidth Unicode, and backslash dot-segments evade forbidden-name checks. Decode to a bounded fixed point, normalize Unicode, and normalize separators before path normalization.
- MED R11 evaluation_core.py:1024: four positive/four negative clusters plus 20 excluded unlabeled rows clear the ten-cluster CI gate as N=28 (8/300 degenerate draws). Filter to metric-contributing observations before counting/resampling clusters.
- MED R12 evaluation_core.py:983: CIResult accepts point=NaN with finite bounds; NaN min_clusters permits a two-cluster CI. Require finite point estimates and finite integer cluster/replicate controls; validate failure tolerances.
- MED R13 evaluation_core.py:1148: PU ablations bound top_k by all rows rather than the PU universe; k=15 with 20 rows/10 candidates aborts with SchemaError instead of recording a blocked quantity. Bound against eligible universe size.
Reproduce from repo root with the specified interpreter and PYTHONPATH=feng/src; each R line is a tiny synthetic script after the shared imports:
```python
from conference.model_v2 import evaluation_core as e; from conference.model_v2.tests.test_evaluation_core import row, independent_rows, labelled; import pytest
r=labelled(10,10); [x.pop('negative_evidence') for x in r[10:]]; t=e.ObservationTable(tuple(r)); print('R1',[e.compute_metric(k,t,[1.]*10+[0.]*10,threshold=.5).value for k in ('auprc','auroc','fdr','accuracy')])
r=labelled(10,0); print('R2',[e.compute_metric(k,r,[1.]*10,policy=e.MetricPolicy(v,1),threshold=.5).value for v in (0,float('nan')) for k in ('auprc','accuracy','fdr')])
r=labelled(10,10); [x.update(study_id='holgersen_s4',provenance={'source':'Holgersen S4'}) for x in r]; print('R3a',e.compute_metric('auroc',r,[1.]*10+[0.]*10).value); [x.update(source_table_kind='responder-only',negative_evidence={'assayed_and_powered':True,'detection_limit':.1,'basis':'absence from responder list'}) for x in r[10:]]; print('R3b',e.compute_metric('auroc',r,[1.]*10+[0.]*10).value)
r=[row('p'+str(i)) for i in range(10)]+[row('n'+str(i),'verified_negative') for i in range(10)]; print('R4',e.compute_metric('auroc',r,[1.]*10+[0.]*10).n_negative_units,len(set(e.effective_clusters(r))))
r=independent_rows(6); r[1]['independent_unit_id']=r[0]['independent_unit_id']; n=e.make_nested_splits(r,outer_mode='leave_study_out'); print('R5',any({r[i]['independent_unit_id'] for i in o.test_idx}&{r[i]['independent_unit_id'] for i in f.train_idx+f.test_idx} for o,fs in zip(n.outer.folds,n.inner) for f in fs))
r=independent_rows(7); [r[i].update(aso_sequence=s) for i,s in enumerate(('A'*18,'A'*16+'CC','A'*14+'CCCC','G'*18))]; r[3].update(start=r[1]['start'],end=r[1]['end']); n=e.make_nested_splits(r,outer_mode='leave_study_out'); g=n.outer.group_ids['sequence']; print('R6',any(g[i]==g[j] for fs in n.inner for f in fs for i in f.test_idx for j in f.train_idx))
r=independent_rows(6); r[0]['chemistry_family']='MOE'; r[1]['chemistry_family']="2'-MOE"; p=e.make_splits(r,'leave_study_out'); print('R7',p.group_ids['chemistry'][:2],1 in p.folds[0].train_idx)
r=labelled(6,6); p=e.make_splits(r,'leave_study_out',n_folds=3); [x.update(aso_sequence=r[0]['aso_sequence']) for x in r]; print('R8',len(e.run_ablation(r,{},'M0',p,policy=e.MetricPolicy(1,1)).cells))
r=labelled(6,6); p=e.make_splits(r,'leave_study_out',n_folds=3); f={x['observation_id']:{'m1_wc_pairs':1.} for x in r}; print('R9',len(e.run_ablation(r,f,'M1',p,lambda tr,te,c:{x['observation_id']:.5 for x in te},policy=e.MetricPolicy(1,1)).cells))
print('R10',[e.check_source_not_forbidden(p) for p in ('%2570si25/a','ｐｓｉ２５/a',r'feng\.\terminal/a')])
r=labelled(4,4,n_unl=20); c=e.bootstrap_metric_ci('auroc',r,[1.]*4+[0.]*24,policy=e.MetricPolicy(1,1),n_boot=300,seed=1); print('R11',c.n_clusters,c.n_failed,len(set(e.effective_clusters(r[:8]))))
r=independent_rows(10); c=e.cluster_bootstrap_ci(r,lambda idx:float('nan') if tuple(idx)==tuple(range(10)) else 1.,n_boot=20); d=e.cluster_bootstrap_ci(independent_rows(2),lambda idx:sum(idx)/len(idx),min_clusters=float('nan'),n_boot=20); print('R12',c.point,c.lower,c.upper,d.n_clusters)
r=labelled(4,3,n_unl=6,n_unassayed=5,n_censored=2); p=e.make_splits(r,'leave_study_out'); print('R13',pytest.raises(e.SchemaError,e.run_ablation,r,{},'M0',p,pu=True,policy=e.MetricPolicy(1,1),top_k=(15,)).value)
